// REJECTS: Field 'content' should be specified only once
//
// Text fields are an unordered repetition in the grammar; "only once" is a walker check,
// reported by name.
//
// Text is the smallest section in the language -- one element, three keywords -- and that
// is precisely why it is worth a negative. It is the section a rewrite implements in an
// afternoon as "read fields until '}'", and that implementation silently accepts a second
// content, keeps the last one, and loses the first without a word.
###Text
Text fixture::neg::TwoBodies
{
   type: 'plainText';
   content: 'first';
   content: 'second';
}
